# Security response headers.
#
# This file is the Cloudflare Pages "_headers" format and only takes effect if
# the site is served by Cloudflare Pages. If the frontend is served another way
# (origin server / Caddy / nginx, or a Cloudflare Transform Rule at the edge),
# set the SAME headers there — a static _headers file is inert off CF Pages.
#
# Clickjacking protection must be an HTTP header: X-Frame-Options and the CSP
# `frame-ancestors` directive are IGNORED when delivered via a <meta> tag.
/*
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
